2026-10-06 16:55:47.778 DEBUG icod.agent.runtime.loop: ========== TURN START ==========\nPROMPT:\n# Smartsheet-Inspired Backend Demo\n\nBuild a backend-only API for a simplified Smartsheet-inspired work management application.\n\nThere should be **no frontend/UI work** in this task. The API will be tested and verified using **cURL and Postman**.\n\nThe goal is to build the core backend architecture for users, workspaces, sheets, rows, and forms.\n\n## Technology Stack\n\nUse the following technologies:\n\n* **Node.js** as the runtime\n* **Express.js** as the backend web framework\n* **PostgreSQL** as the relational database\n* Use a suitable PostgreSQL ORM/query builder such as **Prisma, Drizzle, or Sequelize**\n* Use a secure authentication mechanism suitable for a REST API\n* Use environment variables for configuration and secrets\n\nThe implementation should follow a clean and maintainable backend architecture with clear separation between routes/controllers, business logic, database access, validation, and middleware where appropriate.\n\n## Core Data Hierarchy\n\n```text\nUser\n └── Workspaces\n      ├── Workspace\n      │    ├── Sheets\n      │    │    ├── Columns\n      │    │    ├── Rows\n      │    │    └── Forms\n      │    └── ...\n      │\n      └── ...\n```\n\n## 1. Users\n\nImplement user creation and authentication.\n\nA user should have at least:\n\n* `id`\n* `name`\n* `email`\n* `password` / securely stored password hash\n* timestamps\n\nUsers can own multiple workspaces.\n\nThe relationship should be represented using an `ownerId`/foreign key rather than storing the user's email or name directly.\n\nImplement appropriate API endpoints for:\n\n* Creating a user\n* Authenticating a user\n* Retrieving the authenticated user's information\n\nAuthentication should be implemented so that protected workspace, sheet, and form operations can identify the current user.\n\n## 2. Workspaces\n\nAn authenticated user can create and manage multiple workspaces.\n\nEach workspace belongs to exactly one owner.\n\nA workspace should contain at least:\n\n* `id`\n* `name`\n* `ownerId`\n* timestamps\n\nImplement endpoints for:\n\n* Creating a workspace\n* Listing the authenticated user's workspaces\n* Retrieving a specific workspace\n* Updating a workspace\n* Deleting a workspace\n\nUsers must not be able to access or modify workspaces they do not own.\n\n## 3. Sheets\n\nA workspace can contain multiple sheets.\n\nA sheet should belong to exactly one workspace.\n\nA sheet should contain at least:\n\n* `id`\n* `name`\n* `workspaceId`\n* timestamps\n\nImplement endpoints for:\n\n* Creating a sheet inside a workspace\n* Listing sheets in a workspace\n* Retrieving a specific sheet\n* Updating a sheet\n* Deleting a sheet\n\nThe API should verify that the authenticated user owns the workspace before allowing access to its sheets.\n\n## 4. Sheet Columns\n\nEach sheet should support a basic column structure.\n\nA column should have information such as:\n\n* `id`\n* `sheetId`\n* `name`\n* `type`\n* `position`\n\nInitially support:\n\n* `text`\n* `number`\n* `boolean`\n* `date`\n\nImplement endpoints for creating, updating, deleting, and listing columns.\n\nThe design should allow additional column types to be added later.\n\n## 5. Sheet Rows\n\nSheets should contain rows of data.\n\nA row belongs to a specific sheet.\n\nFor the initial version, rows can contain values corresponding to the sheet's columns.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nSheet Columns:\nName | Email | Status\n\nRow:\nAli | ali@gmail.com | Active\n```\n\nImplement endpoints for:\n\n* Creating a row\n* Listing rows in a sheet\n* Retrieving a row\n* Updating a row\n* Deleting a row\n\nThe API must validate that submitted values correspond to the sheet's defined columns and their types.\n\n## 6. Forms\n\nA form is an input mechanism associated with a specific sheet.\n\nCreating a form should not create a separate data store. Instead, form submissions should ultimately create rows in the associated sheet.\n\nA form should contain information such as:\n\n* `id`\n* `sheetId`\n* `n... (+3384 chars)
